<section class="copy-section" id="understand-what-still-connects-your-digital-lives" aria-labelledby="understand-what-still-connects-your-digital-lives-heading"><div class="wrap copy-body"><h2 id="understand-what-still-connects-your-digital-lives-heading">Understand what still connects your digital lives</h2>
<p>You may have changed a password and still be unsure where access ends. A device, family service or recovery arrangement can connect otherwise separate parts of your digital life.</p>
<p>Dr. Tabansky examines those connections within the agreed scope, including what may still expose private messages, photos, documents or location information. He explains how relevant access persists and which changes need to be considered together. You have someone to work through those connections with you.</p>
<p>Such access can remain without a new intrusion. Its presence does not establish that your spouse has used it or explain how someone learned a particular fact.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="copy-section" id="make-changes-with-their-consequences-in-view" aria-labelledby="make-changes-with-their-consequences-in-view-heading"><div class="wrap copy-body"><h2 id="make-changes-with-their-consequences-in-view-heading">Make changes with their consequences in view</h2>
<p>A password change may leave another route open. Changing a family service can affect access you still need, and some changes generate notifications or become visible to other users.</p>
<p>We explain what the relevant access allows and agree the sequence with you. You can decide what to change with a clearer understanding of the effects. We do not promise invisible changes.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="copy-section copy-offer" id="have-your-own-devices-and-access-examined-with-urgent-first-aid" aria-labelledby="have-your-own-devices-and-access-examined-with-urgent-first-aid-heading"><div class="wrap copy-body"><h2 id="have-your-own-devices-and-access-examined-with-urgent-first-aid-heading">Have your own devices and access examined, with urgent first aid</h2>
<p><strong>Private Exposure Assessment · Typically four hours</strong></p>
<p><strong>₪3,600 including VAT</strong></p>
<p>We inspect the relevant access with you on one main phone and one PC, iPad or second phone, including digital identities, accounts, apps, recovery routes and access to data. We complete the agreed intake, access mapping, diagnosis and approved urgent first aid where safely possible within scope.</p>
<p>You receive a practical summary of what was reviewed, found and changed, what remains and the next steps, even if you buy nothing further. We work only with what is disclosed, observable or otherwise lawfully accessible within your authorized environment and agreed scope.</p>
